  "audio": "short-03.mp3",
  "duration": 28.813061,
  "cues": [
    {
      "index": 97,
      "localStart": 0,
      "localEnd": 2.4,
      "text": "Then the tournament ends. The fans fly home."
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "localStart": 2.4,
      "localEnd": 3.92,
      "text": "And the stadiums stay."
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "localStart": 3.92,
      "localEnd": 7.82,
      "text": "English has a perfect phrase for what happens next: a \"white elephant\"."
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "localStart": 7.82,
      "localEnd": 12.21,
      "text": "A huge, expensive thing you cannot really use - but you must keep feeding."
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "localStart": 12.21,
      "localEnd": 15.82,
      "text": "Brasilia built a stadium that cost at least five hundred fifty million dollars."
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "localStart": 15.82,
      "localEnd": 17.42,
      "text": "Beautiful. Enormous."
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "localStart": 17.42,
      "localEnd": 20.18,
      "text": "One problem: the city has no big football club."
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "localStart": 20.18,
      "localEnd": 25.1,
      "text": "So by 2015, its parking lot was being used... by city buses."
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "localStart": 25.1,
      "localEnd": 26.16,
      "text": "Rows of them."
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "localStart": 26.16,
      "localEnd": 28.78,
      "text": "The stadium was finally full. Full of buses."
    }
  ]
}